@consumer = http://localhost:4131/odata/v4/shop
@provider = http://localhost:4141/odata/v4/provider

### Live proxy — reads are forwarded to the remote provider
GET {{consumer}}/Customers

### Column restriction + renames — only 5 fields, remote price → unitPrice
GET {{consumer}}/Products

### Rename translation flows through $filter (unitPrice → remote price)
GET {{consumer}}/Products?$filter=unitPrice gt 100&$orderby=unitPrice desc

### Entity-level rename — same remote data, Supplier domain
GET {{consumer}}/Suppliers

### Static where — $filter=blocked eq false is injected automatically
GET {{consumer}}/ActiveCustomers

### Compare: the upstream provider directly
GET {{provider}}/Customers

### CUD opt-in — create is forwarded to the remote (writable: true)
POST {{consumer}}/WritableCustomers
Content-Type: application/json

{ "ID": "C999", "name": "Example Co", "city": "Berlin", "country": "DE", "email": "hello@example.co" }

### Selective writes — delete is rejected with 405 (create+update only)
DELETE {{consumer}}/WritableCustomersNoDelete('C999')
